#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-AD0513 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
# Rule:Description: A variable ending in SDTF must have a label that ends with "Imputation Flag" (or "Imput. Flag") and contains "Start" and "Date"
#note "Labels in the shapes of CDISC's own ADaMIG labels: ASDTF spells Imputation in full; XPERSDTF, XSPRSDTF and XP01SDTF (sponsor names shaped as APERSDTF, ASPRSDTF and the template APxxSDTF's AP01SDTF) abbreviate to "Imput." -> all accepted. The real ADaMIG names resolve to their own literal or template rows in the product and are never judged by a stem rule (PLAN-library-template-label-resolution T2 review L4), so the scenario uses sponsor names to stay on the stem leg."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#library variable-metadata ADLBC *SDTF name=*SDTF label="{Start Date Imputation Flag}"
#library variable-metadata ADLBC *DTF name=*DTF label="{Date Imputation Flag}"
#library variable-metadata ADSL TRTSDTF name=TRTSDTF label="Date of First Exposure Imput. Flag"
#library variable-metadata ADSL TRxxSDTF name=TRxxSDTF label="Date 1st Exposure Period xx Imput. Flag"
dataset ADLBC class=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col ASDTF type=Char label="Analysis Start Date Imputation Flag"
col XPERSDTF type=Char label="Period Start Date Imput. Flag"
col XSPRSDTF type=Char label="Subperiod Start Date Imput. Flag"
col XP01SDTF type=Char label="Period 01 Start Date Imput. Flag"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALB | x | x | x | x
---
